{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>מאהל</b> Four times in the Masorah: ויצא מאהל לאה. מאהל מועד לאמר. ואהיה מתהלך מאהל אל אהל. יתצך לנצח ויסחך מאהל. Meaning: when the Tabernacle was established, the high places (במות) were forbidden — that is ויקרא אליו מאהל מועד, specifically. After they crossed the Jordan, the high places were permitted until they came to Shiloh — that is ויצא מאהל לאה, i.e., the Tabernacle that Bezalel made, who came from the tribe of Judah, who emerged from Leah. ויבא באהל רחל — this is Shiloh, in the portion of Joseph. Then ואהיה מתהלך מאהל אל אהל — from Shiloh to Nov, from Nov to Givon, and from there to the Eternal House (בית עולמים), and then the high places were forbidden — that is יתצך לנצח ויסחך מאהל — there was no permit at all. My lord my father, the Rosh, of blessed memory:"], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :register {:flags {0 ["the Eternal"]}}, :notes {0 "The four Masorah citations are left unaddressed as Ba'al HaTurim gives no verse references for them. The first (ויצא מאהל לאה) is the lemma verse itself, Genesis 31:33; the others are from Leviticus 1:1, Zechariah 3:7, and Hosea 2:11 respectively."}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:25:13.097907728Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}